            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked where the Kentucky Supreme Court said it looked at the subjective state of mind of police."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e864eca0a453-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked what objections exist to adding the alternative phrase \"or in bad faith\"."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer argued that the lower court was wrong because it treated police tactics that foreseeably create exigent circumstances as irrelevant to reasonableness."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e864eca0a453-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether the Court should decide the question of whether police may create exigent circumstances and use them to enter."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked what the discussion of police officers' lawfulness has to do with the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether it is unlawful for a police officer to threaten to burst into a home."
      }
