        ],
        "text": "According to Kentucky, the case addresses how the Fourth Amendment applies when police create the very circumstances that justify a warrantless entry, potentially expanding or limiting police powers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e864eca0a453-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, conversely, the respondent\u2019s position that police may rely on any ensuing exigency could broaden police authority to act pre\u2011emptively, raising concerns about civil liberties."
      }
